# Overview
#
# One word in a redundant pair already carries the other, so the reader
# reads a word that adds nothing. This tier reports `still remain`,
# where `remain` alone usually carries the meaning. The fix deletes
# `still`. The rule sits at Recommended, because `still` can stress that
# a state outlasted an event.
#
# Expression
#
# `$remain` expands to remain, remains, remained, and remaining through
# Harper's dictionary.
#
# Related Rules
#
# The Required ProseRedundantPair holds every other redundant pair.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 1 line in the measure.py corpus, and 0 of 1 sampled hits
# needed the fix. In the one misfire, `still` stressed that a default
# outlasts a release (`will still remain Disabled, for backwards
# compatibility`), a contrast that `remain` alone does not carry.
expr main still $remain
let message "Redundant pair. Delete the word the other one includes."
let description "Flags `still remain`, where `remain` alone usually carries the meaning."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The lock remains held after Close."
allows "Three entries survive the sweep."
